{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And Joseph said: This is what I spoke to you, saying: You are spies.</b> And let me now renew a second proof on this matter, for it is difficult for me: why is this younger brother not with you? Rather, he was surely here with you and went on his way, for he had already heard some novelty in this place, and you sent him to your sender to report what he had already heard, while you remained here to spy further. And by this you shall be tested: you shall bring your younger brother here, and I will investigate whether they have already seen him in this place or not — for if they have not seen him here, then your words are honest; and if you do not bring him, by the life of Pharaoh, you are spies, for you fear lest someone testify about him that they already saw him in this city and he went off alone. And according to this approach it is possible to explain that everything is one single allegation, and he adduced two proofs upon it: for first he said, 'You are spies,' since you hid yourselves among those who came in, and furthermore he adduced a second proof, for 'the nakedness of the land you have come to see,' for you entered through ten gates of the city. And they said, 'No, my lord,' and so on, 'We are all the sons of one man,' and so on — and with this they explained their concealment, saying: we are afraid of the evil eye. And he said to them, 'No, but the nakedness of the land you have come to see' — and the word 'כִּי' functions as 'הָרֵי,' and he said to them: even granting the explanation that you offered for your concealment, in any case how can you say that you are not spies, when plainly the nakedness of the land you have come to see — from which part the city is vulnerable to conquest? Therefore they responded to both: 'We are all the sons of one man' to explain the concealment, and 'one is not' to explain the entry through ten gates of the city. This is the matter that I spoke, as is explained in the first approach, and this explanation is more sufficient than the explanation of the Akeidah and Mahar'i[a] in resolving all the difficulties and the matter of the test concerning the younger brother. And some say that he fabricated the allegation of spying against them because he feared lest they investigate who the ruler is and it become known to them that he is Joseph."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "העקידה refers to the Akeidat Yitzchak (R. Isaac Arama); מהרי״א is an abbreviation likely for a commentator's name, left unresolved with abbreviation mark retained."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:33:12.024010597Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}